      "body": "<!-- Thank you for your contribution! Please follow these guidelines to enhance your pull request. If anything is unclear, submit your PR and reach out to maintainers for assistance. Join our Slack community at https://slack.sglang.io to discuss further. -->\n\n<!-- PR title: [Type] scope: title, or [Type] [Hardware] scope: title.\nType: Feat, Fix, Refactor, Perf, Doc, Test, CI, or Chore.\nScope: any module or model name (no fixed list or letter-case restriction), e.g. attention, qwen3, or flash-attn.\nHardware: optional single tag without spaces. Use uppercase hardware tags (AMD, NVIDIA, NPU, MI300X), except for exactly these four spellings: Intel, Apple, Huawei, Ascend.\nTitle: no letter-case restriction.\nReverts: use GitHub's default title, Revert \"original title\".\nExamples: [Fix] attention: Fix KV cache indexing; [Perf] [AMD] flash-attn: Optimize decode performance. -->\n\n## Motivation\n\n<!-- Describe the purpose and goals of this pull request. -->\n`--enable-torch-compile` cannot finish startup on DeepSeek-V4 / V4.1. During decode\nCUDA graph capture, Inductor precompiles the mHC sinkhorn kernel and fails:\n```\nTriton compilation failed: _hc_mix_reduce_sinkhorn_kernel_0\ntriton.compiler.errors.CompilationError: at 1:0:\ndef _hc_mix_reduce_sinkhorn_kernel(\n^\nAttributeError(\"'NoneType' object has no attribute '_unflatten_ir'\")\n```\n\n_hc_mix_reduce_sinkhorn_kernel declares part_mix_residual_ptr=None, and its two non-residual call sites omit the argument. torch's Triton-kernel higher-order operator does not bind an omitted parameter to its declared default, so the parameter is recorded with a None type and Triton's code generator fails on it. PyTorch has a fix for the general problem in progress: pytorch/pytorch#201081 (bind omitted Triton kernel params to their declared defaults).\n\n\n\n## Modifications\n\n<!-- Detail the changes made in this pull request. -->\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n<!-- If this pull request affects model outputs (e.g., changes to the kernel or model forward code), provide accuracy test results. -->\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n<!-- If this pull request impacts inference speed, provide benchmarking and profiling results. -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40287055478](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40287055478)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40287055374](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40287055374)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40287055456](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40287055456)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
